# Environment files.
#
# `.env.*` matches .env.production.template and .env.test.template as well as
# the real .env.production / .env.test. There is deliberately NO
# `!.env.*.template` negation here: these templates currently contain a live
# service_role key (bypasses RLS) and a live sk_live_ Paystack secret key
# (can move real money), and a template is by definition committed.
#
# To share the structure, commit a SANITIZED copy under a name that is not
# matched by this block, e.g. supabase/env.production.example, with every
# value blank. Keep secrets only in the ignored .env.production / .env.test.
.env
.env.*
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
coverage/
.vscode/
*.pem
*.key
supabase/.temp/
supabase/.branches/
supabase/.env
supabase/functions/**/*.zip
